{"answerArea":{"calculator":false,"chi2Table":false,"periodicTable":false,"tTable":false,"zTable":false},"hints":[{"content":"We can expand this expression like any product of two binomials. However, this expression has a special form that makes it easier to expand.\n\nThis is the \"difference of squares\" form (where $P$ and $Q$ can be any monomial):\n\n$(P+Q)(P-Q)=P^2-Q^2$\n\n[[☃ explanation 1]]","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{"explanation 1":{"alignment":"default","graded":true,"options":{"explanation":"$\\begin{align}\n\u0026\\phantom{=}(P+Q)(P-Q)\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=P(P-Q)+Q(P-Q)\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=P^2-\\cancel{P\\cdot Q}+\\cancel{Q\\cdot P}-Q^2\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=P^2-Q^2\n\\end{align}$","hidePrompt":"Got it, thanks!","showPrompt":"Show me why this is true.","static":false,"widgets":{}},"static":false,"type":"explanation","version":{"major":0,"minor":0}}}},{"content":"$\\begin{align}\n\u0026\\phantom{=}(5-2x^4)(5+2x^4)\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=(5)^2-\\left(2x^4\\right)^2\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=25-4x^{8}\n\\end{align}$","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}}],"itemDataVersion":{"major":0,"minor":1},"question":{"content":"** Expand and combine like terms.**\n\n$(5-2x^4)(5+2x^4)=$ [[☃ expression 1]]","images":{},"widgets":{"expression 1":{"alignment":"default","graded":true,"options":{"answerForms":[{"considered":"correct","form":true,"key":0,"simplify":false,"value":"-4x^8+25"}],"buttonSets":["basic","prealgebra"],"functions":["f","g","h"],"times":false},"static":false,"type":"expression","version":{"major":1,"minor":0}}}}}
